# ヲ格名詞句と述語の共起 — the dependency criterion.
#
# The `where` counterpart to `sketch_wo_predicate` in `sketch-grammar.sgx`.
# That relation is a LINEAR rule — a nominal, を, at most five gap tokens that
# are not verbs, auxiliaries, punctuation or competing particles, then a
# predicate — and its header records the false-positive shape it cannot
# avoid: an argument governed by an intervening predicate (Nを対象にVを実施)
# attaches to the wrong verb, and anything more than five tokens away is
# never reached. This catalog states the fact the linear rule approximates:
# the を-marked nominal is a dependent of the predicate, whatever lies between
# them. It requires `dep.head` and `dep.rel` (CoNLL-U input or a
# dependency-parsing analyzer) and is refused at binding otherwise, by name.
#
# The two catalogs are the two arms of
# `docs/results/2026-09-14-wo-predicate-dependency-comparison/README.md`,
# which joins their records on the character position of the を particle
# itself — the one token both tokenizations agree on — and classifies every
# を-phrase as found by both with the same predicate, found by both with
# different predicates, or found by one arm only.
#
# Tagset note (GiNZA 5.2 / UD Japanese). A サ変 stem followed by する is
# tagged VERB on the stem (勉強/VERB し/AUX), so `[upos=VERB]` reaches the
# same predicates the linear rule spells as `[unidic.pos1=名詞 &
# unidic.pos3=サ変可能] [lemma=為る]`. The を particle carries `case` to the
# nominal it marks; the nominal carries its argument relation to the
# predicate. `WO_PHRASE_ROLE` is the class of relations a を-marked nominal
# can bear to its governor, not the inventory this catalog has observed —
# projecting `$collocate.dep.rel` in the key is what turns that inventory
# into measured output rather than an authored assumption (the discipline
# `double-wo-dep.sgx` adopted after its label-set re-validation).
#
# `wo_predicate_linear` is the linear rule restated over the same CoNLL-U
# tokens, so the comparison's primary arm pair differs in exactly one thing —
# adjacency versus dependency — and joins by token index. GiNZA's XPOS column
# is the UniDic tag string (`名詞-普通名詞-一般`, `助詞-格助詞`), which lets
# `sk_nominal`, `sk_wo`, `sk_gap` and `sk_predicate` be spelled as anchored
# regexes over `xpos`. It is a restatement, not the tracked catalog: GiNZA
# segments in Sudachi mode C, so a compound the UniDic rule sees as several
# tokens is one token here, and する after a サ変 stem carries `lemma=する`
# where UniDic carries 為る. The record measures the tracked Vibrato arm
# separately, by character alignment, so that difference is reported rather
# than hidden.
#
# Two recorded limits, both language facts rather than choices here. SGX has
# no negative edge between two named captures, so "no closer predicate
# governs this nominal" cannot be written and is not needed: a nominal has
# exactly one `dep.head`, so at most one `$head` assignment passes per
# を-phrase. And a `where` clause filters the assignments the body admits —
# `[]*` admits every later verb as a candidate head, the clause keeps the
# one the parse names, and the per-start selection then publishes it.

defaults
  source: "research query, ヲ格名詞句と述語の共起 dependency criterion"
  status: "experimental"
end

# Nominal heads a を phrase can have. NUM is included because 三つを選ぶ is a
# を-marked argument like any other.
set WO_DEP_NOMINAL := {NOUN, PROPN, PRON, NUM}.

# The relations a を-marked nominal can bear to its governor: UD's core
# arguments, its clausal and nominal dependents, and `dep`.
set WO_PHRASE_ROLE := {obj, obl, iobj, nsubj, csubj, ccomp, xcomp,
                       advcl, acl, nmod, dep}.

# The linear rule over CoNLL-U tokens. Fragment names mirror
# `sketch-grammar.sgx`; every predicate is an XPOS prefix.
role: "helper"
fragment wo_lin_nominal :=
  [xpos ~ /\A(名詞|代名詞)/]
  ([xpos ~ /\A接尾辞-名詞的/])*.

role: "helper"
fragment wo_lin_wo := [text=を & xpos ~ /\A助詞-格助詞/].

# The gap also excludes a サ変 stem, as the published query does and
# `sk_gap` does not: without it 発見した parses as gap 発見 + head し, and the
# key names する where the reader wants 発見.
role: "helper"
fragment wo_lin_gap :=
  [xpos !~ /\A(動詞|助動詞|補助記号)/
   & xpos !~ /\A助詞-(格助詞|係助詞|接続助詞)/
   & xpos !~ /サ変可能/].

role: "helper"
fragment wo_lin_predicate :=
  ( [xpos ~ /\A名詞-普通名詞-サ変可能/] [lemma=する]
  | [xpos ~ /\A動詞/] ).

role: "research"
category: "ヲ格共起"
relation: "noun_wo+V"
head: "predicate"
collocate: "accusative"
key: [$head.first.lemma, $collocate.span.lemma]
pattern wo_predicate_linear :=
  (?<collocate> @wo_lin_nominal)
  @wo_lin_wo
  (@wo_lin_gap){0,5}
  (?<head> @wo_lin_predicate).

# The pair is a projection, not a declaration: `$collocate.dep.rel` is the
# label its own edge matched, so `summarize` reports which of
# `WO_PHRASE_ROLE`'s members held, as data.
role: "research"
category: "ヲ格共起"
relation: "noun_wo+V"
head: "predicate"
collocate: "accusative"
key: [$head.lemma, $collocate.lemma, $collocate.dep.rel]
pattern wo_predicate_dep :=
  (?<collocate> [upos in @WO_DEP_NOMINAL])
  (?<w> [text=を & upos=ADP])
  []*
  (?<head> [upos=VERB])
  where $collocate -[case]-> $w, $head -[@WO_PHRASE_ROLE]-> $collocate.
